00:08:14.055 --> 00:08:16.527
- Yeah, I'm not professional
at all, I'm just real.

00:08:16.527 --> 00:08:19.199
This is an important lesson, be real.

00:08:19.199 --> 00:08:21.778
Be honest, don't be
afraid of making mistakes,

00:08:21.778 --> 00:08:24.524
don't be afraid of
showing who you truly are,

00:08:24.524 --> 00:08:26.217
I know there's a lot of people that think,

00:08:26.217 --> 00:08:29.261
oh you have to wear like a
fancy tie and suit all the time

00:08:29.261 --> 00:08:30.595
and you can't make mistakes

00:08:30.595 --> 00:08:32.217
and you have to be so
prepared for everything,

00:08:32.217 --> 00:08:34.023
that's not realistic, okay.

00:08:34.023 --> 00:08:36.750
The more real you are,
the better you'll do

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:38.653
in whatever field you are.

00:08:38.653 --> 00:08:40.330
We're all human, okay?

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:43.107
Skynet doesn't take over the
world for another few decades.

00:08:43.107 --> 00:08:46.164
So for right now, we're all that's here.

00:08:46.164 --> 00:08:48.396
We're the kings and queens of this world.

00:08:48.396 --> 00:08:50.922
So just act human, and
you might be surprised

00:08:50.922 --> 00:08:52.705
at how people react to you.

00:08:52.705 --> 00:08:55.440
- You start to look, what
can I do to get happy?

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:59.287
It's not just about money,
it's about self sufficiency,

00:08:59.287 --> 00:09:01.037
and finding yourself.

00:09:02.213 --> 00:09:04.060
And for me it's not, you know,

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:06.927
I took 12,000, I'm now at 4.5
million in trading profits,

00:09:06.927 --> 00:09:09.404
that's cool, but the journey along the way

00:09:09.404 --> 00:09:11.677
helped me find myself and build myself.

00:09:11.677 --> 00:09:13.592
And I chose not to work on Wall Street

00:09:13.592 --> 00:09:15.054
but to travel all over the world

00:09:15.054 --> 00:09:16.458
because I love that personally.

00:09:16.458 --> 00:09:18.687
Try different stuff but see how it feels.

00:09:18.687 --> 00:09:20.711
I want more people
thinking like scientists,

00:09:20.711 --> 00:09:22.327
like testing testing testing,

00:09:22.327 --> 00:09:23.928
refining refining refining.

00:09:23.928 --> 00:09:26.237
But you got to break the rat race cycle,

00:09:26.237 --> 00:09:28.975
where it's just like money
is going to solve everything.

00:09:28.975 --> 00:09:29.808
It won't.

00:09:29.808 --> 00:09:30.767
- Yeah, I hear you.

00:09:30.767 --> 00:09:32.621
- Even though I teach how
to make money, that's,

00:09:32.621 --> 00:09:34.755
you know, it's kind of contradictory.

00:09:34.755 --> 00:09:36.212
Some people are like, well why do you--

00:09:36.212 --> 00:09:37.837
- We want to make money
to have some flexibility

00:09:37.837 --> 00:09:40.325
and freedom in our lives,
but it's not everything.

00:09:40.325 --> 00:09:42.229
- Exactly, you need to
get out of, you know,

00:09:42.229 --> 00:09:43.656
working for somebody else's dream.

00:09:43.656 --> 00:09:45.628
So if you have a little
savings or some money,

00:09:45.628 --> 00:09:47.178
then you're working on your own dreams.

00:09:47.178 --> 00:09:48.264
- [Host] Right right, exactly.

00:09:48.264 --> 00:09:51.188
- Why do you think you
were so good at investing?

00:09:51.188 --> 00:09:53.227
- Um, at first I was
actually trying to invest

00:09:53.227 --> 00:09:56.311
in big companies but my
portfolio wasn't really moving.

00:09:56.311 --> 00:09:59.896
So I gravitated towards lower
price stocks, penny stocks.

00:09:59.896 --> 00:10:01.869
And that really got my accounts moving.

00:10:01.869 --> 00:10:03.545
They're more volatile, they're riskier,

00:10:03.545 --> 00:10:04.759
but they're simpler.

00:10:04.759 --> 00:10:07.147
They usually have one or
two products, you know,

00:10:07.147 --> 00:10:09.383
so they're either going to
succeed big or fail big.

00:10:09.383 --> 00:10:11.840
So what I try and do is ride the momentum

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:13.285
for a few days or a few hours

00:10:13.285 --> 00:10:14.927
when they announce good
news, a big partnership,

00:10:14.927 --> 00:10:16.975
or something like that,
and I make my money grow,

00:10:16.975 --> 00:10:18.291
like you were talking about earlier,

00:10:18.291 --> 00:10:20.455
you know, trying to make $10 or $100.

00:10:20.455 --> 00:10:22.766
So I keep it simple and I'm always focused

00:10:22.766 --> 00:10:24.472
on the big goal at the end,

00:10:24.472 --> 00:10:26.686
but I'm taking small
profits along the way.

00:10:26.686 --> 00:10:28.957
- The key to being successful

00:10:28.957 --> 00:10:31.219
is to work harder than other people.

00:10:31.219 --> 00:10:33.024
Because everybody wants success.

00:10:33.024 --> 00:10:36.012
Everybody wants a Lamborghini,
everybody wants freedom.

00:10:36.012 --> 00:10:39.762
But, what are you willing
to do to get there?

00:10:40.769 --> 00:10:42.711
That's my question to you, you know.

00:10:42.711 --> 00:10:44.875
We're here at the most
prestigious university

00:10:44.875 --> 00:10:47.319
in America, Harvard, fantastic.

00:10:47.319 --> 00:10:50.046
I'm very honored, thank
you for having me here.

00:10:50.046 --> 00:10:51.816
The people who have gotten here

00:10:51.816 --> 00:10:53.865
have worked their butts off to get here.

00:10:53.865 --> 00:10:55.805
But that's just the beginning.

00:10:55.805 --> 00:10:58.538
Whether you're in college or
you're going to go to college

00:10:58.538 --> 00:11:00.373
or you're out of college,

00:11:00.373 --> 00:11:02.330
this is a lifelong
journey where you have to

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:05.328
continually work hard, work
harder than other people,

00:11:05.328 --> 00:11:06.964
to get ahead.

00:11:06.964 --> 00:11:10.528
A lot of people give
up at different times.

00:11:10.528 --> 00:11:13.012
I'm not longer at that stage, you know.

00:11:13.012 --> 00:11:16.351
When I had my big loss,
I basically gave up.

00:11:16.351 --> 00:11:18.283
For a year I was in the gutter.

00:11:18.283 --> 00:11:20.278
But I came back and I said, you know what,

00:11:20.278 --> 00:11:22.769
this was a mistake that I made investing.

00:11:22.769 --> 00:11:24.137
It wasn't the patterns.

00:11:24.137 --> 00:11:25.652
I didn't go against what I had learned

00:11:25.652 --> 00:11:28.528
to make all my millions before this loss.

00:11:28.528 --> 00:11:30.150
I invested.

00:11:30.150 --> 00:11:32.913
And I didn't do my full due diligence.

00:11:32.913 --> 00:11:34.667
And that was my mistake.

00:11:34.667 --> 00:11:36.296
I eventually got back into trading,

00:11:36.296 --> 00:11:37.786
I saw more patterns,

00:11:37.786 --> 00:11:39.879
and I became the number one ranked trader

00:11:39.879 --> 00:11:42.748
out of 50,000 on Covestor in 2007 to 2011.

